se\n   wrapping_shl only if the C code genuinely relies on it, otherwise plain <<).\n4. Pointer walking: keep the same pointer arithmetic with `.add(1)`/`.sub(1)`\n   and `.offset_from()`. `*s++ = c` -> `*s = c; s = s.add(1);`\n   `*--s == '9'` -> `{ s = s.sub(1); *s == b'9' as c_char }`.\n   Characters: `'0' + dig` -> `(b'0' as c_int + dig) as c_char`.\n5. Goto: the function uses labels\n   `use_exact, no_div, ulp_reached, Roundup, retc, ret1, no_digits, one_digit,\n    toobig, Fast_failed, Fast_failed1, bump_up, ret, ret_ ...`\n   Model them faithfully. A clean way: write the body as a `loop { ... }` state\n   machine, or use labelled blocks (`'lab: loop { ... break 'lab; }`).\n   Correctness of control flow is the most important thing in this task.\n   Double-check every goto target.\n6. `switch(Rounding)` where Rounding==1: the preprocessed code shows\n   `switch(1) { case 0: ...; case 2: ...; }` — neither case matches, so that\n   statement is a NO-OP; translate it as nothing (but keep any code that follows).\n7. Keep the C variable names.\n8. Every `Bfree`, `Balloc`, `mult`, `diff`, ... call must be kept in the same\n   order — allocation order is observable.\n9. `if (!buf) { buf = rv_alloc(i); blen = sizeof(Bigint) + ((1 << ((int*)buf)[-1]) - 1)*sizeof(ULong) - sizeof(int); }`\n   translate as: `buf = rv_alloc(i); blen = std::mem::size_of::<Bigint>() + (((1usize << *(buf as *const c_int).sub(1)) - 1) * std::mem::size_of::<ULong>()) - std::mem::size_of::<c_int>();`\n   (size_of::<Bigint>() is 32.)\n10. Do not add any tests, no `main`, no `mod tests`.\n\n## Verification you must do before reporting back\nRun:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/translated_rust && cargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -40\nOther modules of the crate may still be incomplete/broken (other agents are\nworking on them) — that is expected. What you MUST ensure is that there are ZERO\ncompile errors reported for `src/dtoa_r.rs`. Iterate until `cargo build` sh