{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yjfujxkrw2elpk4zmzdfg4fxtkei3ickjeop6ws6pxr6dadxv23q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Deliverable\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/translated_rust/src/dtoa_r.rs` — **1097 lines**, exports `dtoa_r` with the required signature.\n\n## Compile status\n`cargo build --release` finishes successfully. **Zero** output lines mentioning `dtoa_r.rs` — no errors, no warnings from that file. (The only warning in the whole crate is a pre-existing `unnecessary unsafe block` at `src/dtoa.rs:150`, not mine.)\n\n## How the translation was done\n- The C goto web is modelled as an explicit state machine `loop { match state { ... } }` labelled `'sm`, with one state per C label: `UseExact, NoDiv, UlpReached, Roundup, Toobig, FastFailed, FastFailed1, NoDigits, OneDigit, Round9Up, Roundoff, Ret, Retc, Ret1`. `use_exact1`, `accept_dig` and `more96` are handled inline (`use_exact1` sets `s=buf; i=1` then transitions to `UseExact`; `accept_dig` and `more96` are Rust labelled blocks) because they are only ever entered from within the same loop iteration.\n- All `u64` arithmetic uses `wrapping_*`; shifts stay as `<<`/`>>`.\n- `switch(Rounding)` with `Rounding == 1` translated as a no-op comment, code after it kept.\n- Allocation order (`Balloc`/`Bfree`/`mult`/`diff`/`pow5mult`/`multadd`/`lshift`) preserved exactly, including the short-circuit in `if (ilim < 0 || cmp(b, S = multadd(S,5,0)) <= 0)`.\n- Constant-table reads (`Lhint`, `pten`, `pfive`, `pfivebits`) use raw-pointer offsets, not slice indexing, so no bounds-check panics are introduced where C does unchecked subscripting.\n\n## Key finding worth flagging\nThe C source contains a **reachable out-of-bounds read**: `if ((dbits >> 11) > (pfive[k-1] << j))` is executed with `k == 0` for `mode` 3/5/7/9 with `ndigits == -1` and `1 <= |d| < 10`. I verified in the compiled C library (`tmp/cbuild/libjansson.so`) that `pfive[]` sits at a `0x100`-aligned offset preceded by zero padding, so `pfive[-1]` reads `0`. The Rust `pfive()` accessor therefore returns `0` for negative indices (documented in a comment). Without this, Rust either panics or reads different adjacent memory and takes the `no_digits` branch instead of `one_digit` — this was the sole source of 144 mismatches in my differential test before the fix.\n\n## Differential verification against the C build\nI built three C harnesses that `dlopen` both `tmp/cbuild/libjansson.so` (original C) and `translated_rust/target/release/libjansson.so` (this port) and compared `dtoa_r` (and `dtoa`) return value, buffer contents, `*decpt`, `*sign`, and `*rve` offset:\n\n| run | coverage | comparisons | mismatches |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | fixed corner values, all 2098 powers of two, all powers of ten, 60k random bit patterns; modes 0-9, ndigits 0-22, plus small `blen` (1-25) to exercise the `blen <= i` NULL-return path | 23,879,200 | 0 |\n| 2 | negative ndigits (-40..40), all modes, incl. the `buf == NULL` malloc path via `dtoa()`+`freedtoa()` | 4,946,260 | 0 |\n| 3 | 120k random (bits, mode -1..10, ndigits -50..69, random blen), plus `nextafter` neighbours of every power of two and power of ten | 530,124 | 0 |\n\nTotal ~29.4M cases, 0 mismatches. Infinity/NaN/±0, denormals (incl. `5e-324`), `1e308`, mode clamping (`mode<0||mode>9`), `mode>5` folding, and the `spec_case` power-of-two boundary paths are all covered. Temporary test files were removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":777,"cache_read_input_tokens":115808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":777,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012szMKVzUrtCaFU9huwGMp8","session_id":"6fbb13b3-6d71-4b14-8197-54b0f0754899","uuid":"9ce8b4dd-356c-4334-80ca-3cc0d125b32e","timestamp