harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/tmp/strtod_only.c\n  (744 lines, contains ONLY this one function)\n\nRead it in three or four chunks, e.g. Read(offset 1 limit 200),\nRead(offset 200 limit 200), Read(offset 400 limit 200), Read(offset 600 limit 150).\nDo NOT try to read a 700+ line range in one call.\n\nThe labels used in the C body are:\n  break2, have_dig, dig_done, ret0, ret, ovfl, range_err, undfl, many_digits,\n  denormal, denormal1, tiniest, smallest_normal, roundup, roundup1, noround,\n  noround1, drop_down, cont\nMap them faithfully. Recommended approach: an explicit state machine\n`let mut st = St::...; loop { match st { ... } }` with one variant per label that\nis the target of a backward jump or of jumps from several places, and Rust\nlabelled blocks (`'lbl: { ... break 'lbl; }`) for pure forward jumps. `goto ret`\nappears from many places and is the common exit: the cleanest structure is\n```rust\n'ret: loop {            // or a labelled block\n    ...  break 'ret;    // == goto ret\n}\n/* ret: */ if !se.is_null() { *se = s as *mut c_char; }\nreturn if sign != 0 { -rv.dval() } else { rv.dval() };\n```\nMake sure `goto ret0` (which sets `s = s00`) is distinguished from `goto ret`.\n\n## The Rust API you must build on (already written -- do NOT modify)\nRead this file first:\n  /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/tmp/DTOA_API.md\nIt gives the exact Rust names/signatures for: Bigint, U, BCinfo, Balloc, Bfree,\nbx (== b->x), multadd, mult, pow5mult, lshift, cmp, diff, d2b, b2d, ratio,\nquorem, dshift, increment, rshift, any_on, s2b, hi0bits, lo0bits, i2b, ulp,\nand the tables TENS/BIGTENS/TINYTENS/HEXDIG/PFIVE, and the already-translated\nhelpers match_(), hexnan(), gethex(), sulp(), bigcomp(), plus the constants\nRound_zero/Round_near/Round_up/Round_down and all the IEEE_8087 #defines\n(Exp_shift, Exp_msk1, Exp_mask, P, Bias, Emin, Emax, Exp_1, Frac_mask, LSB,\nSign_bit, Big0, Big1, Ten_pmax, Quick_max, Int_max, Bletch, Log2P, Tiny0, Tiny1,\nDBL_DIG, DBL_MAX_10_EXP, DBL_MAX_EXP, Rounding, strtod_diglim, Nbits, Ebits,\nBndry_mask, Bndry_mask1, Frac_mask1, Exp_msk11, Exp_shift1, Exp_11).\nYou may also read src/dtoa.rs and src/dtoa_strtod.rs to confirm signatures.\n\n## Translation rules (follow strictly)\n1. `word0(&rv)` -> `rv.w0()`, `word1(&rv)` -> `rv.w1()`, assignments ->\n   `rv.set_w0(v)` / `rv.set_w1(v)`; `dval(&rv)` -> `rv.dval()`,\n   `dval(&rv) = v` -> `rv.set_dval(v)`; `rv.d` -> `rv.dval()`.\n   The preprocessed source writes `(&rv)->L[1]` for word0 (HIGH word) and\n   `(&rv)->L[0]` for word1 (LOW word) -- do not mix them up.\n   `(&rv)->L[1] &= ~0x80000000;` means `rv.set_w0(rv.w0() & !0x80000000)`.\n2. `b->x` -> `bx(b)` (a `*mut u32`); `b->x[i]` -> `*bx(b).add(i as usize)`;\n   `b->wds` -> `(*b).wds`, etc.\n3. `tens[i]` -> `TENS[i as usize]`, `bigtens[i]` -> `BIGTENS[i as usize]`,\n   `tinytens[i]` -> `TINYTENS[i as usize]`, `hexdig[c]` -> `HEXDIG[c as usize]`.\n   `(*__errno_location ()) = 34;` -> `libc::set_errno(libc::ERANGE);`.\n4. Types: `ULong`->`u32`, `Long`/`int`->`c_int`, `unsigned long long`->`u64`,\n   `double`->`f64`. Use `wrapping_add/sub/mul` wherever C integer arithmetic\n   could overflow. Keep `<<`/`>>` as-is.\n5. Pointers stay pointers: `const char *s` -> `*const c_char`; walking with\n   `.add(1)`/`.sub(1)`; `s - s0` -> `s.offset_from(s0) as c_int`.\n   `c = *s` where `int c` -> `let c = *s as c_int;` (C sign-extends char, so\n   `as c_int` from `c_char`(i8) is correct). Where the C code casts to\n   `const unsigned char *` use `*(p as *const u8) as c_int`.\n   `for(s = s00;;s++)` etc. stay literal.\n6. Keep every C variable name; keep statement/allocation order exactly\n   (Balloc/Bfree/mult/diff/... call order is observable).\n7. Do NOT add tests, no `main`, no `mod tests`, no `#[cfg(test)]`.\n8. Where C reads an uninitialised local on some path, initialise it to 0 in Rust\n   (add a `/* C leaves this uninitialised */` comment).\n\n## Verification you MUST do before reporting\n1. `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/translated_rust && cargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -40`\n   Iterate until the whole crate builds with ZERO errors.\n2. Confirm the symbol appears:\n   `nm -D --defined-only target/release/libjansson.so | grep strtod__unused`\n3. Differential test against the original C library. Write your test program\n   under $TMPDIR (never in the repo), e.g. $TMPDIR/sdtest/t.c, that dlopen()s\n   BOTH shared objects:\n     C   : /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/tmp/cbuild/libjansson.so\n     Rust: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/translated_rust/target/release/libjansson.so\n   resolves `strtod__unused` from each with dlsym, and compares, for a few\n   thousand inputs, (a) the returned double's exact bit pattern, (b) the end\n   pointer offset, (c) errno after the call. Cover: plain decimals, many random\n   digit strings of length 1..60 with random exponents, hex floats\n   (\"0x1p3\", \"0X1.8p-5\", \"0x.8p1\", \"0x1.fffffffffffffp+1023\"), \"inf\",\n   \"infinity\", \"INF\", \"nan\", \"nan(0x1234)\", \"-nan\", leading whitespace and\n   signs, garbage suffixes, empty string, \"e5\", \".\", \"1e\", \"1e+\", \"0x\",\n   subnormal/overflow/underflow edges (\"5e-324\", \"2.4703282292062327e-324\",\n   \"1e-323\", \"1.7976931348623157e308\", \"1e309\", \"1e-400\"), and long digit\n   strings that exercise the >= 40-digit (strtod_diglim/bigcomp) path such as\n   \"0.500000000000000000000000000000000000000000001\" and\n   \"9007199254740993.0000000000000000000000000000001\".\n   Compile with `gcc -w -O0 ... -ldl -lm`.\n   Iterate on your Rust until there are ZERO mismatches.\n4. Delete your temporary test files afterwards (they are outside the repo anyway).\n\nReport: line count of src/dtoa_strtod2.rs, the build status, the number of\ndifferential cases tested and the number of mismatches (must be 0)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null