{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a4622b6264428a687","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GT5r18obKaxzYouPwZv49x","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-uh3rjz-translated-rust/6fbb13b3-6d71-4b14-8197-54b0f0754899/tasks/a4622b6264428a687.output","summary":"Done.\n\n## Deliverable\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-uh3rjz/translated_rust/src/dtoa_strtod2.rs` — **1223 lines**, exports exactly one item: `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn strtod__unused(s00: *const c_char, se: *mut *mut c_char) -> f64` (plus a private `enum St`). No other file was created or edited; `src/lib.rs` already contained `pub mod dtoa_strtod2;` (line 13).\n\n## Build\n`cargo build --release`: **0 errors, 0 warnings** attributable to the new file. Symbol confirmed:\n`0000000000022060 T strtod__unused` in `target/release/libjansson.so`.\n\n## Differential test vs. the original C library\n**3,699,693 cases, 0 mismatches** on (bit pattern of returned double, end-pointer offset, errno). Both `.so`s were `dlopen`ed with `RTLD_LOCAL` and the symbol resolved with `dlsym` from each handle (verified with `dladdr` that the two resolve into different libraries, including their internal `gethex`).\n\nCorpora: the full fixed list requested (whitespace/signs, `\"\"`, `\"e5\"`, `\".\"`, `\"1e\"`, `\"1e+\"`, `\"0x\"`, inf/infinity/nan/nan(0x1234), hex floats, subnormal/overflow/underflow edges, the 40+-digit bigcomp cases), plus randomized: 1..60-digit mantissas with random exponents, 38..85-digit mantissas (bigcomp path), hex floats, exponents swept through ±280..±360, garbage byte strings, `%.*g`/`%.*e`/`%.60f` round-trips of random bit patterns, and exact decimal expansions (computed with `Fraction`) of doubles, of midpoints between adjacent doubles, and of `2^k` for k in −1400..1024 with last-digit perturbations. Both `se = &ptr` and `se = NULL` were exercised.\n\n## Structure / notes\n- `goto ret` is a labelled `'ret: loop`; the labels `ret0, denormal, denormal1, tiniest, smallest_normal, roundup, roundup1, noround, noround1, many_digits, ovfl, range_err, undfl` are variants of an `enum St` dispatched by that loop (fall-through, e.g. `roundup → noround` and `ovfl → range_err`, is reproduced by setting the next state). Pure forward jumps use labelled blocks: `'break2`, `'dig_done`, `'drop_down`/`'after_drop_down`, `'cont`; `goto have_dig` is a loop-entry flag.\n- Harness validation: I injected mutations and confirmed the tests detect them (e.g. XOR-1 in `noround` → 373 439 mismatches). I then temporarily instrumented the file with an exported counter array and confirmed coverage of every label including the rare ones: `denormal`(32 918), `denormal1`(36 347), `tiniest`(722), `smallest_normal`(2), `drop_down`(5 146 via `i<0`, 124 via the `i==0` fall-through), `goto cont`(5 083), `req_bigcomp`/`bigcomp`(41 372), `sulp` ±(345), the `bc.scale`/`aadj2` rescale path(6 858), `ovfl`/`undfl`/`range_err`. The instrumentation was then removed.\n- Five branches proved unreachable by construction and were verified by line-by-line inspection instead: the `if (Lsb1)` *then*-branch and the `bc.uflchk = 1` inside `if (i == 0)` (both require `bc.nd > nd` together with `i == 0`, which the preceding `if (bc.nd > nd && i <= 0)` makes impossible — dead in the C too); the `bc.uflchk = 1` in `drop_down` and in the `rv.L[0]==1 && !rv.L[1]` case; and the `goto cont` in the `y == Big0-exponent` branch.\n- Two C constructs needing care, both documented in comments: `1 << i` / `1ull << i` (int/u64 shifts that C leaves UB for large `i`; only evaluated when `nd > 19`, where `i <= 4`) and `0xffffffff << (2*P+1-(y>>20))` — I masked the shift counts (`& 31` / `& 63`) so Rust reproduces gcc/x86 semantics exactly rather than panicking or emitting poison.","usage":{"total_tokens":180526,"tool_uses":45,"duration_ms":1490019},"uuid":"d8cc0973-a143-44e0-a2a5-0b681adfcc16","session_id":"6fbb13b3-6d71-4b14-8197-54b0f0754899"}
